# 6. PHASE D — CONTACT ARCHITECTURE

The contact model must remain global.

Conceptually:

```text
PERSON
  |
  +-- Company Association A
  |     title
  |     team
  |     whyThisPerson
  |     evidence
  |     conversationAngle
  |
  +-- Company Association B
        title
        team
        whyThisPerson
        evidence
        conversationAngle
```

A person should not become duplicated merely because they belong to multiple companies.

---

# 6.1 Contact type

Support:

```text
PERSON
ROLE_ADDRESS
```

Examples:

### PERSON

```text
Jane Doe
jane@company.com
VP Engineering
```

### ROLE_ADDRESS

```text
Engineering Hiring
engineering@company.com
```

The UI should clearly distinguish them.

---

# 6.2 Reference URL

Support optional:

```text
Reference URL
```

Examples:

* LinkedIn
* company team page
* job posting
* conference profile
* article
* company announcement

Persist it.

Display it appropriately on contact detail.

---

# 6.3 Add contact from company

This is still incomplete.

From a company context:

```text
Company
→ Contacts
→ Add contact
```

The user must be able to:

### Option A

Create a new person.

### Option B

Find an existing global person and associate them with this company.

The second path is critical.

Example:

```text
Search existing contacts
[ Jane Doe                    ]
[ John Smith                  ]
[ Sarah Williams              ]
```

Selecting Jane should create/update the company association rather than duplicate Jane globally.

---

# 6.4 Duplicate detection

Improve duplicate detection.

At minimum:

* exact email match
* normalized email comparison
* obvious existing-person match warning

Do not prevent legitimate role addresses from being added.

---

# 6.5 Editing

Editing must work for:

### Global person data

Examples:

* name
* email
* LinkedIn/reference URL

Changes should update the global person.

### Company-specific association

Examples:

* role/title
* team
* why this person
* evidence
* conversation angle

Changes should only update that company relationship.

Make this distinction clear in the UI.

