# 9. COMPANY OUTREACH TAB

Company detail must have a genuine Outreach tab.

It must show only:

```text
outreaches where outreach.companyId === currentCompany.id
```

Do not show all global outreaches.

Each row should identify:

```text
Contact
Subject
Status
Created/Sent
Campaign
Conversation
```

Clicking opens the global outreach detail route.

---

# 10. COMPANY CAMPAIGNS TAB

The company Campaigns tab must be properly scoped.

It should show campaigns where at least one campaign member belongs to the current company.

Conceptually:

```text
Campaign
  members
    ↓
  contact
    ↓
  company association
    ↓
  current company
```

Do not filter campaigns merely by campaign name or a manually stored company ID if the real relationship is membership-based.

If the prototype model needs a denormalized company reference for UX, keep it consistent with membership.

---

# 11. COMPANY CONVERSATIONS TAB

Company Conversations must only show conversations involving contacts associated with that company.

Do not show unrelated global conversations.

Global:

```text
/conversations
```

shows all.

Company:

```text
/company/:id → Conversations
```

shows only company-related conversations.

Conversation detail remains the existing canonical conversation detail experience.

---

# 12. CONVERSATION SEPARATION

Audit the entire conversation model.

Conversation is:

```text
a thread of messages exchanged with a contact
```

It can originate from:

* manual outreach
* campaign outreach
* inbound reply
* manually recorded interaction

It must not require a campaign.

It must not equal an outreach.

---

## Required message model behavior

A conversation can contain:

```text
OUTREACH
FOLLOW_UP
CONTACT_REPLY
USER_REPLY
```

or the existing equivalent.

The conversation timeline must remain coherent.

If an outreach is sent and a contact replies:

```text
Outreach
→ Conversation
→ Contact reply
```

If the user sends a reply:

```text
Conversation
→ USER_REPLY
```

Do not create a second conversation unnecessarily.

---

