# 15. CAMPAIGN SENDER ACCOUNT SELECTION

Campaign creation must support selecting a sender account.

Display:

```text
Sender:
Jane Doe <jane@example.com>

Via:
Resend Production
```

Persist:

```text
campaign.senderAccountId
```

Every campaign-created outreach should inherit that sender account unless intentionally overridden by an explicit product rule.

---

# 16. SENDER ACCOUNT DAILY LIMIT

The previous pass added a UI field but this must become meaningful state.

Sender account should support:

```text
dailyLimit
sentToday
```

or equivalent.

When sending simulated messages:

```text
sentToday < dailyLimit
```

allows sending.

When:

```text
sentToday >= dailyLimit
```

sending is blocked.

Show a clear state:

```text
Daily sending limit reached

This sender account has reached its configured limit of 50 messages today.
```

Do not silently increment beyond the limit.

---

# 16.1 Reset behavior

For a prototype, you may implement a simulated day boundary based on stored date:

```text
sentTodayDate
```

If the date changes, reset the simulated daily count.

Do not require a real backend scheduler.

---

# 17. INTEGRATIONS

The previous implementation missed Integration Name.

An Integration should support something equivalent to:

```ts
Integration {
  id
  name
  provider
  status
}
```

Example:

```text
Resend Production
Resend
Connected
```

Multiple integrations must be supported.

Example:

```text
Resend Production
Resend Sandbox
SMTP Personal
SMTP Work
```

Do not assume only one integration can exist.

---

# 17.1 Integration name

Add:

```text
Integration Name *
```

This is the user-facing identity.

Do not use the provider name as the only identity.

---

# 17.2 Test Connection

Keep this simulated.

Required states:

```text
Idle
Testing
Success
Failed
```

Button:

**Test connection**

Do not call real provider APIs.

A successful simulated test should update visible status appropriately.

A failed simulated test should be understandable and recoverable.

