# 33. END-TO-END ACCEPTANCE SCENARIOS

Actually perform these flows in the prototype.

## Scenario A — New user skips onboarding

```text
Signup
→ Onboarding
→ Skip
→ Dashboard
→ incomplete profile banner
→ Complete profile
→ banner disappears
```

---

## Scenario B — Company lifecycle

```text
Add company
→ enter all fields
→ save
→ company list shows values
→ open company
→ values visible
→ edit
→ values update
→ navigate away
→ return
→ values still correct
→ archive
→ confirmation
→ company becomes archived
→ active list excludes it
→ archived filter shows it
```

---

## Scenario C — Existing person association

```text
Company A
→ Add Contact
→ search existing person
→ select person
→ add company association
→ Company A shows person

Company B
→ Add Contact
→ same person
→ associate

Global Contacts
→ person appears once

Person detail
→ Company A association
→ Company B association
```

---

## Scenario D — Individual outreach

```text
Company
→ Contacts
→ Prepare outreach
→ Outreach draft created
→ correct contact/company
→ edit subject/message
→ save
→ navigate away
→ return
→ draft still exists
→ mark ready
→ send
→ status becomes SENT
```

---

## Scenario E — Outreach → Conversation

```text
SENT outreach
→ contact replies
→ conversation created/linked
→ conversation status REPLIED
→ not automatically ACTIVE
→ user chooses Continue conversation
→ ACTIVE
```

---

## Scenario F — Multiple contacts

```text
Company
→ Contact A
→ Prepare outreach
→ Outreach A

Company
→ Contact B
→ Prepare outreach
→ Outreach B

Global Outreaches
→ A and B both appear separately

Company Outreach
→ both appear

Neither overwrites the other
```

---

## Scenario G — Campaign

```text
Create campaign
→ select multiple contacts
→ select template
→ select sender account
→ review
→ create
→ campaign members persist
→ company Campaigns shows campaign when appropriate
→ individual outreaches can be traced back to campaign
```

---

## Scenario H — Sender limit

```text
Sender account daily limit = 2

Send outreach 1
→ 1/2

Send outreach 2
→ 2/2

Attempt outreach 3
→ blocked
→ clear explanation
```

---

## Scenario I — Integration

```text
Add integration
→ Integration Name
→ Provider
→ save
→ appears in integrations list
→ Test connection
→ Testing
→ Success
```

Multiple integrations must coexist.

