# 34. FINAL VERIFICATION

Before declaring completion:

Run the project's available validation/build/type checks.

Then manually inspect the major workflows.

Do not report:

> "Implemented"

merely because:

* the route exists
* the component renders
* TypeScript passes

The acceptance standard is:

```text
DATA CREATED
+
DATA PERSISTED
+
DATA SHOWN
+
DATA LINKED
+
USER CAN CONTINUE THE WORKFLOW
```

For each major feature verify all five.

---

# 35. FINAL RESPONSE FORMAT

When finished, report:

## Implemented

List the concrete functionality actually completed.

## Fixed From Previous Pass

Explicitly identify the previously claimed-but-incomplete features that are now genuinely fixed.

## Additional Issues Found

List any issues you discovered beyond my supplied list and what you fixed.

## Remaining Limitations

Only list limitations that genuinely remain.

## Validation

Report:

* TypeScript/build result
* routes checked
* persistence checked
* major end-to-end flows checked
* responsive/accessibility checks performed

Do not claim something passed if you did not actually verify it.

Most importantly:

**Do not stop at analysis or planning. Implement the fixes.**
